      "Map each coding query closure value to its source: the request record for the request, the source document for the check, and the chart for the surviving destination value. Keep a version label on every file that can change. Name the repository where sensitive evidence is held. Compare the source and the destination values before drawing a conclusion. In the coding query closure queue, an item without a next action is treated as an exception. For this coding query closure case, Outsourced Billing Services asks the billing specialist to write the open question and the named approver before the claim moves.",
      "A short written rule is easier to test than an unwritten habit. Link each value to the field or page that supports it. Name the repository where sensitive evidence is held. If the team cannot reproduce the result from the record, the control is not finished. For coding query closure, the working file keeps the request record and the source document beside the decision note. For this coding query closure case, Outsourced Billing Services asks the billing specialist to write the open question and the named approver before the claim moves.",
      "## Definitions and measures",
      "The coding lead owns the decision in coding query closure; the preparer may compare, label, and route but may not approve the outcome. A role change should trigger a review of queue access. Do not let a deadline expand a role beyond its written limit. A case that moves between owners should keep both owner periods visible. The coding query closure close note cites the chart, the approver, and the time of the final check. The Outsourced Billing Services review ties each coding query closure correction to the original claim record in the chart instead of replacing it.",
      "Keep emergency authority narrow and followed by a review note. Do not let a deadline expand a role beyond its written limit. If the team cannot reproduce the result from the record, the control is not finished. A role change should trigger a review of queue access. The coding query closure case note should show what the chart held at the time and who reviewed it. The Outsourced Billing Services review ties each coding query closure correction to the original claim record in the chart instead of replacing it.",
      "## Evidence dictionary",
      "Each morning the team reviews coding query closure arrivals, items waiting on the coding lead, and items ready for a verified close. A case with no next action is an exception even if it says in progress. Keep the queue view readable on one screen. A case that moves between owners should keep both owner periods visible. A sample coding query closure review checks the request record, the source document, and the surviving value in the chart. Outsourced Billing Services treats a missing the request record as an open item, not as a passed check.",
      "A short written rule is easier to test than an unwritten habit. Escalate an item that has waited past the written threshold. Do not let a status update stand in for a verified event. Compare arrivals and completions, not only the backlog total. Apply the same coding query closure test to the reviewer note and to the value that survives in the chart. Outsourced Billing Services treats a missing the request record as an open item, not as a passed check.",
      "## Sampling and collection",
      "If the record does not match the surviving value, stop the dependent action and log the conflict in the chart rather than choosing the more convenient value. Keep the original request so a later correction does not erase the reason for the work. If the team cannot reproduce the result from the record, the control is not finished. The record should show the source, the decision, and the surviving value in one place. In this coding query closure case, the record points to the chart and names the coding lead as the decision owner. A coding query closure handoff at Outsourced Billing Services ends only when the next reviewer can act from the written record.",
      "A case that moves between owners should keep both owner periods visible. The next reviewer should not have to ask which document is authoritative. The record should show the source, the decision, and the surviving value in one place. A clean-looking status is not evidence that the underlying work is correct. The coding query closure reviewer records the close entry, the owner, and the next action in one place. A coding query closure handoff at Outsourced Billing Services ends only when the next reviewer can act from the written record.",
      "## Analysis and reporting",
      "Record the coding query closure close reason, the approver, and the surviving evidence reference in the same case note. Name the owner for every open item, including items waiting on someone else. The record should show the source, the decision, and the surviving value in one place. Do not let a deadline expand a role beyond its written limit. For coding query closure, the working file keeps the request record and the source document beside the decision note. At Outsourced Billing Services, the coding query closure queue marks a held claim with the reason it stopped and the person who can release it.",
      "A case that moves between owners should keep both owner periods visible. Do not mark complete until the check is repeatable by another reviewer. Verify that the surviving record is the one downstream teams will use. Note the next review date before closing. Every coding query closure handoff names the coding lead and the field in the chart that will confirm the change. At Outsourced Billing Services, the coding query closure queue marks a held claim with the reason it stopped and the person who can release it.",
      "## Limitations",
      "Review coding query closure with a sample drawn from the queue export before the meeting, so the discussion cannot drift to memorable cases. Keep the original request so a later correction does not erase the reason for the work. Use the same definition across the queue and the review so the counts agree. Name the owner for every open item, including items waiting on someone else. The coding query closure case note should show what the chart held at the time and who reviewed it. Outsourced Billing Services keeps the coding query closure source, reviewer, and decision date together in the chart so a later check does not depend on memory.",
      "Set the next review date before the action begins. The record should show the source, the decision, and the surviving value in one place. Report age and dependency, not only the total count. Include a routine case, a reopened case, and a cross-owner handoff. For coding query closure, compare the request record with the destination value rather than relying on a status label. Outsourced Billing Services keeps the coding query closure source, reviewer, and decision date together in the chart so a later check does not depend on memory.",
      "## Review and next action",
      "The coding query closure working paper should show the request, the source, the decision, the action, and the surviving value without a private inbox. Write the note so a reviewer can reconstruct the decision without a meeting. Use the approved repository for sensitive content. The next reviewer should not have to ask which document is authoritative. Apply the same coding query closure test to the reviewer note and to the value that survives in the chart. For this coding query closure case, Outsourced Billing Services asks the billing specialist to write the open question and the named approver before the claim moves.",
      "A clean-looking status is not evidence that the underlying work is correct. Use the same definition across the queue and the review so the counts agree. Do not store credentials or unnecessary personal data in the case. Record event time separately from entry time. The coding query closure record should let a second reviewer rebuild the decision from the source document and the reviewer note. For this coding query closure case, Outsourced Billing Services asks the billing specialist to write the open question and the named approver before the claim moves.",
      "## Sources and review limits",
      "The sources below describe the billing, privacy, and recordkeeping context for this protocol, not a result for this sample. The review compares [the prior authorization workflow](/blog/check-a-payer-contract-carve-out-before-the-claim-posts) and [the credit balance review](/blog/set-a-weekly-remittance-posting-reconciliation) with this measurement. Each reference is checked against the publisher page on the observation date and kept beside the working file. Findings remain local operational evidence and do not replace a coding, compliance, or contract review. See [CMS: Medicare Claims Processing Manual](https://www.cms.gov/regulations-and-guidance/guidance/manuals/internet-only-manuals-ioms-items/cms018912), [CMS: National Correct Coding Initiative](https://www.cms.gov/medicare/coding-billing/national-correct-coding-initiative-ncci-edits), and [GAO Green Book](https://www.gao.gov/products/gao-14-704g) for the governing context."
